@*
    The Settings page's Personas tab: read-only paths to where this installation keeps its
    Persona files and its SQLite database, for hand-editing a Persona file, backing up team.db,
    or pointing run.ps1 -Clean's own comment at the same two locations. Nothing here is editable -
    this tab shows facts, it does not change them - so, unlike Appearance, it has no local state,
    no store subscription and no save path.

    The Persona path is resolved through TeammatePaths, the same helper PersonaStore's own
    constructor uses, rather than a public property on PersonaStore itself. The database path is
    computed the same way SqliteTeamDirectory's own constructor computes it (Path.Combine off
    TeamOptions.DataDir, which ServiceCollectionExtensions' PostConfigure<TeamOptions> has already
    resolved to an absolute path by the time any IOptions consumer - this component included -
    sees it), rather than exposed as a public property: SqliteTeamDirectory's connection string is
    private, and adding a public accessor for one read-only settings paragraph is more surface
    than this needs.
*@

@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Acp
@inject IOptions<TeamOptions> Options
@inject TeammatePaths TeammatePaths

<p class="teammates-intro">
    Persona files and the room database live in plain folders and files on disk, so you can back
    them up, hand-edit a Persona, or copy them to another installation without going through the
    application.
</p>

<p class="settings-prompts-file-path">
    Persona files are stored at <code>@this.TeamsDirPath</code>, one Markdown file per Persona,
    Team sub-folders included.
</p>

<p class="settings-prompts-file-path">
    The room database is stored at <code>@this.DbPath</code>.
</p>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// Where <see cref="Agency.Huddle.App.Acp.PersonaStore"/> scans for and watches Persona
    /// Markdown files - <see cref="TeammatePaths.DefinitionsRoot"/>, the same helper its own
    /// constructor uses.
    /// </summary>
    private string TeamsDirPath => this.TeammatePaths.DefinitionsRoot;

    /// <summary>
    /// Where <see cref="Agency.Huddle.App.Data.SqliteTeamDirectory"/> opens the room database -
    /// the same <c>Path.Combine(DataDir, "team.db")</c> its own constructor computes.
    /// </summary>
    private string DbPath => Path.Combine(this.Options.Value.DataDir, "team.db");
}
